{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["These are the heads of their fathers' houses — the Mekhilta explains: these are the three tribes that Jacob censured at the time of his testament; Scripture now traces their lineage to make known that they are important. And according to the plain sense: it was necessary to trace the lineage here up to Moshe and Aharon, and up to Korah and the sons of Uzziel and Pinehas — those mentioned in the Torah before us — so that we know who they are, those mentioned before us."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:31.423841261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}